\[
\begin{array}{c|cccccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{1} & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\
\cline{2-7}
2 & 199 & \downarrow & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{198} & & & & & \\
\cline{2-2}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{1} & 9 & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 8 & & & & \\
\cline{3-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 1 & 1 & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 1 & 0 & & & \\
\cline{4-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 1 & 0 & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 1 & 0 & & \\
\cline{5-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 0 & 0 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 0 & 0 & \\
\cline{6-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & & 0 & 0 \\
\end{array}
\]
So, $199_{10}$ in base 2 is $11001111_2$.
